     A*                                     JUBADD - deliberately mis-typed
     A*                                     "staging" file for 05-11 (decimal
     A*                                     data error). Same field names/
     A*                                     lengths as db/v1/juchud.pf's
     A*                                     JUCHDR record EXCEPT JUSU, which
     A*                                     is 5A here instead of JUCHUD's
     A*                                     5S 0 - same total record length
     A*                                     (27 bytes) but a different type
     A*                                     for that one field.
     A*
     A*                                     Used by src/qclsrc/c0511s.clp with
     A*                                     CPYF FMTOPT(*NOCHK): FMTOPT(*NOCHK)
     A*                                     copies records between mismatched
     A*                                     formats without the normal field-
     A*                                     type check, so a row inserted here
     A*                                     lands its raw character bytes in
     A*                                     JUCHUD.JUSU once copied across -
     A*                                     simulating the *NOCHK-caused
     A*                                     corruption path the 05-11 syllabus
     A*                                     entry names. FIXED (2026-09-27,
     A*                                     real hardware, 2 rounds): JUSU=
     A*                                     'ABCDE' was tried first - EBCDIC
     A*                                     'A'-'E' (X'C1'-X'C5') is actually a
     A*                                     VALID positive zoned-decimal
     A*                                     encoding of +12345 (digit nibbles
     A*                                     1-5, sign nibble C) - no decimal-
     A*                                     data error at all. JUSU=5 blanks
     A*                                     (X'40', zone/sign nibble 4) was
     A*                                     tried next on the assumption an
     A*                                     invalid sign nibble would trigger
     A*                                     it - ALSO no error (JUSU read as
     A*                                     0). Both values happen to share
     A*                                     valid DIGIT (low) nibbles (0-9) on
     A*                                     every byte; the actual trigger for
     A*                                     a real decimal-data error on this
     A*                                     hardware is still unconfirmed -
     A*                                     see docs/probes.md for the current
     A*                                     plan (screen candidate byte
     A*                                     patterns via SQL before spending
     A*                                     another connection on a guess).
     A          R JUCHDR                    TEXT('05-11 mis-typed staging')
     A            JUNO           6A         TEXT('Order number')
     A            JULINE         3S 0       TEXT('Line number')
     A            JUSHO          6A         TEXT('Product code')
     A            JUSU           5A         TEXT('Quantity (5A on purpose)')
     A            JUTNK          7S 2       TEXT('Unit price at order time')
     A          K JUNO
     A          K JULINE
